# Steering Principles

## The Golden Rule
> If new code follows existing patterns, steering should not need updating.

## What belongs in steering
- Organizational patterns, naming conventions, import strategies.
- Architectural decisions and their rationale.
- Technology standards and version policy.
- Security, testing, observability, API conventions.

## What does NOT belong
- File listings or directory dumps.
- Implementation details derivable from the code.
- Secrets, tokens, credentials, customer data.
- Agent-specific tooling internals.

## Per-file checklist
- [ ] One domain per file.
- [ ] Descriptive name.
- [ ] Includes the "why", not just the rule.
- [ ] Includes before/after examples where they clarify.
- [ ] Reviewed during architecture changes.
